      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "1:00 PM: Symposium committee meets to finalize event details and assign duties to the supporting staff, ensuring accountability and testing of AV equipment.\n\n1:30 PM: Gate opens for the keynote speakers and VIP guests, providing a ten-minute grace period.\n\n2:00 PM: Welcome that includes speeches by the organizing committee, introduction of speakers, and an overview of the event.\n\n2:15 PM: Keynote Speaker 1 takes the stage. The audience and attendees focus on absorbing the keynote from on-stage and in the AV displays.\n\n2:25 PM: Keynote Speaker 1 concludes their presentation and allows for Q&A, building anticipation for the next talk.\n\n2:30 PM: Break for refreshments, with more of the symposium materials handed out to attendees, including informational brochures and pre-symposium materials.\n\n2:35 PM: Keynote Speaker 2 steps up, immediately followed by their presentation. Attendees pay close attention to new information and concepts presented.\n\n2:45 PM: Another Q&A session, with a focus on clarifying outstanding questions from the morning's lectures/talks, to enhance attendee understanding.\n\n2:50 PM: Keynote Speaker 2 concludes the afternoon segment, transitioning to open discussion or reflection, preparing attendees",
